WEBVTT

00:05.255 --> 00:08.717
[hip-hop music playing
distantly]

00:09.968 --> 00:11.261
[wind blowing]

00:11.261 --> 00:14.055
[lively chatter nearby]

00:14.055 --> 00:16.182
[traffic hums in background]

00:21.980 --> 00:22.814
Hi.

00:22.939 --> 00:24.315
I know, I know.

00:24.441 --> 00:25.358
I'm late.

00:25.358 --> 00:27.318
- Don't kill me.
- No promises.

00:29.863 --> 00:32.115
You ready?
Everyone's already on the roof.

00:32.115 --> 00:34.492
I, uh... I gotta drop
this off real quick.

00:34.617 --> 00:35.827
But I'm gonna--

00:36.494 --> 00:37.954
I'm gonna m-meet you up there.

00:37.954 --> 00:39.122
- Okay?
- Alright.

00:39.122 --> 00:40.206
Alright.

00:40.957 --> 00:42.500
- Be quick.
- [Victor] I will.

00:43.043 --> 00:44.544
[distant siren wailing]

00:45.920 --> 00:47.839
[reporter] We begin with
some breaking political news

00:47.964 --> 00:49.382
on this Tuesday election night.

00:49.507 --> 00:51.217
Twenty-eight-year-old candidate
Bella Reál

00:51.217 --> 00:52.802
is ahead of Acting Mayor Tomlin

00:52.802 --> 00:54.637
- by huge margins...
- [door opens]

00:54.637 --> 00:55.638
[Victor] Hey.

00:55.638 --> 00:58.016
[woman speaking Spanish]

00:58.141 --> 00:59.309
Hey, Ma.

00:59.309 --> 01:01.895
[speaking Spanish]

01:02.020 --> 01:03.813
[speaking Spanish]

01:03.813 --> 01:06.733
Oof! [speaking Spanish]

01:06.858 --> 01:07.859
[laughing]

01:07.984 --> 01:09.527
[man speaking Spanish]

01:11.529 --> 01:13.531
[in English] Just remember,
it's called arroz borracho,

01:13.656 --> 01:14.908
not esposo borracho.

01:15.700 --> 01:16.534
[mother exclaims]

01:16.659 --> 01:17.869
[chuckling]

01:17.994 --> 01:19.621
[Victor] These parts were
hard to find, Pá.

01:19.621 --> 01:21.164
- Did you get them?
- I think so.

01:21.164 --> 01:23.375
You... wanted one of those, right?

01:23.375 --> 01:24.542
[father] Ah, bueno.

01:24.668 --> 01:28.254
Y... f... forty-twos.
Like you said.

01:28.254 --> 01:30.715
Ah, bien. Good man.

01:32.884 --> 01:34.219
[father sighs]

01:34.344 --> 01:35.637
[Victor] Hooked it up.

01:35.637 --> 01:38.807
[father chopping rapidly]

01:39.516 --> 01:40.475
[clicks tongue]

01:42.852 --> 01:45.689
You know, M-Manny should

01:45.689 --> 01:48.566
really be paying
you extra, you know.

01:48.692 --> 01:50.902
- For finding special parts.
- [food sizzling]

01:51.027 --> 01:53.238
I mean, the guy's got,
like, three garages.

01:53.738 --> 01:54.906
It could be real money for us.

01:55.031 --> 01:56.449
Manny pays me well enough.

01:56.449 --> 01:57.701
[girl] Vic is right.

01:57.701 --> 01:59.202
He's taking advantage
of you, Papi.

01:59.202 --> 02:00.412
You see?

02:00.537 --> 02:03.123
You act like wanting more
is a bad thing,

02:03.123 --> 02:06.376
but, I mean, don't you want
a better life than this?

02:06.376 --> 02:07.585
Victor.

02:08.545 --> 02:10.505
If you remembered
where we came from,

02:10.505 --> 02:12.590
we have more than enough.

02:12.716 --> 02:15.802
[pop music playing faintly]

02:17.595 --> 02:19.264
[phone buzzing]

02:20.890 --> 02:23.226
[Victor] Okay, uh, G-Graciela's
waiting for me.

02:23.226 --> 02:24.269
I gotta go.

02:24.769 --> 02:26.771
- What about dinner?
- Invite her here.

02:26.896 --> 02:28.273
- We have a lot of food.
- No, no, no.

02:28.398 --> 02:29.482
We'll-- I'll eat later.

02:29.482 --> 02:32.277
C-City Hall's setting off
fireworks f...

02:33.111 --> 02:35.363
for the election so we're just
gonna watch from her roof.

02:35.363 --> 02:37.157
Is Calvin going to be there?

02:37.741 --> 02:39.951
Pá, you don't even know him.

02:40.076 --> 02:42.871
- I know his cousin pushes drugs.
- Okay, so?

02:43.663 --> 02:44.789
Calvin's n...

02:45.915 --> 02:47.751
- not a part of Squid's crew.
- [scoffs]

02:47.751 --> 02:50.337
Can't you just chill out
for once

02:50.337 --> 02:52.297
- and let me see my friends?
- Fine.

02:53.256 --> 02:54.883
- Go.
- Alright.

02:54.883 --> 02:55.842
God.

02:58.345 --> 03:00.430
- [door opens, slams shut]
- [mother speaks Spanish]

03:00.430 --> 03:03.558
- [helicopter whirs]
- ...the guy then hops the curb.

03:03.558 --> 03:05.769
He's now skating down
the sidewalk.

03:05.769 --> 03:07.520
The owner's still chasing him.

03:07.520 --> 03:10.106
Now a dog starts
chasing them too.

03:10.106 --> 03:12.484
And then he turns a corner
and blam!

03:13.026 --> 03:15.570
- A semi slams right into him.
- Was the guy okay?

03:15.570 --> 03:16.905
No. He's dead.

03:17.447 --> 03:19.657
- The dog too.
- Yo! [laughs]

03:20.658 --> 03:21.826
Why are you telling us this?

03:21.951 --> 03:23.828
'Cause it was fucked up?
I don't know.

03:23.953 --> 03:24.871
[man] Calvin!

03:25.997 --> 03:27.415
Ayo!

03:27.874 --> 03:29.417
[Calvin] Ayo, Squid!

03:29.417 --> 03:31.503
- [Squid] Calvin, what up, kid?
- What's up, boy?

03:31.628 --> 03:33.672
- [Squid] How you doing?
- [Calvin] Good.

03:33.797 --> 03:35.465
- Got your re-up.
- You got that good good?

03:35.465 --> 03:37.425
- Thank you. Appreciate it.
- For you, man.

03:38.510 --> 03:39.636
What up, Victor?

03:39.636 --> 03:42.305
[all chattering]

03:42.305 --> 03:43.473
[distant siren wailing]

03:43.473 --> 03:44.933
[Graciela] I hate Squid.

03:44.933 --> 03:46.685
[Victor] Yeah, I know. Sorry.

03:46.810 --> 03:48.353
I didn't know he'd be here.

03:48.478 --> 03:50.522
I can't wait to get
out of this shithole.

03:51.648 --> 03:54.025
You should get some flowers,

03:54.693 --> 03:56.861
l-like I got over at my place.

03:56.986 --> 03:58.029
R-really...

03:59.030 --> 04:02.242
Really brightens up
the brick walls.

04:04.577 --> 04:05.537
[Graciela] Mm.

04:06.913 --> 04:08.206
But I dunno.

04:10.500 --> 04:11.918
From up here...

04:14.337 --> 04:15.964
it's kinda nice.

04:16.673 --> 04:18.383
That's 'cause you're
looking far away,

04:18.508 --> 04:20.010
at the rich neighborhoods.

04:20.010 --> 04:21.970
If you were out there
looking back at Crown Point

04:21.970 --> 04:24.014
you'd say,
"Man, what a shithole."

04:24.014 --> 04:27.142
[laughs] Come on,
I like it here.

04:28.435 --> 04:30.562
You know, I do.
This city, it's...

04:33.690 --> 04:34.858
This city's wild.

04:37.068 --> 04:38.737
It's like anything could happen.

04:40.363 --> 04:41.906
Is this you trying to be smooth?

04:42.032 --> 04:43.408
[Victor laughs softly]

04:53.126 --> 04:55.086
Is it working?

04:56.755 --> 04:58.381
- [loud booming]
- [friends cheering]

04:58.381 --> 04:59.632
The show's starting.

05:01.217 --> 05:02.344
[explosion booms nearby]

05:04.429 --> 05:06.306
- [man 1] Oh, my God!
- [man 2] Holy shit!

05:06.306 --> 05:08.558
- [explosions booming]
- [distant screams]

05:08.558 --> 05:09.851
Are those bombs?

05:09.851 --> 05:11.311
God, they're everywhere.

05:11.311 --> 05:13.021
- [booming nearby]
- Whoa! Get down!

05:13.021 --> 05:14.773
[car alarms wailing]

05:14.898 --> 05:16.775
[sirens wailing]

05:16.900 --> 05:18.526
[rumbling]

05:18.526 --> 05:20.862
[high-pitched vibrations
sounding]

05:20.862 --> 05:22.614
[somber, emotional music
playing]

05:22.739 --> 05:24.449
[loud booming]

05:25.158 --> 05:27.952
- [music swells]
- [booming fades]

05:31.915 --> 05:35.210
[low rumbling]

05:38.755 --> 05:42.008
[somber music continues]

05:43.259 --> 05:45.345
[inaudible]

05:48.348 --> 05:50.809
[water whooshing and crashing]

05:50.934 --> 05:52.811
[whooshing fades]

05:55.021 --> 05:58.983
[thunder rumbling]

06:00.276 --> 06:02.445
[rain pattering]

06:02.445 --> 06:04.322
[music fades]

06:08.702 --> 06:10.578
Gettin' forehead grease
all over my window, kid.

06:14.332 --> 06:15.250
Sorry.

06:15.792 --> 06:17.502
Tonight's the night, Vic.

06:18.545 --> 06:20.422
Sofia's
an elusive fuckin' broad,

06:20.422 --> 06:22.924
but she's leadin' us into
a goldmine with Al's new drug.

06:23.633 --> 06:26.177
So then... you and, uh--
you and... and...

06:26.845 --> 06:28.513
S-Sofia, is that like...

06:29.180 --> 06:32.475
Are we, uh,
kinda... partners now?

06:32.475 --> 06:33.893
Temporarily. Um...

06:34.477 --> 06:37.063
Once Luca figures out that
she don't wanna play nice,

06:37.063 --> 06:38.815
the Falcones will
take care of her for us.

06:38.815 --> 06:41.443
But by then, I'll be runnin'
the whole damn trade.

06:41.443 --> 06:43.820
- Isn't Luca her cousin?
- [Oz] Uncle?

06:43.820 --> 06:45.947
All these fucks are related,
you know?

06:45.947 --> 06:48.408
I mean, 60 years ago,
two Sicilian brothers

06:48.533 --> 06:50.160
jizzed all over
the toe of that boot,

06:50.160 --> 06:53.288
now I got three dozen Falcones
breathin' down my neck.

06:56.708 --> 06:57.876
Kid.

06:58.668 --> 06:59.878
Where's your head at?

07:00.754 --> 07:02.589
You still worked up about
that jewel shit?

07:02.589 --> 07:05.592
As far as I'm concerned,
it's ancient history.

07:05.717 --> 07:07.802
I mean, you fucked up. Huge.

07:08.928 --> 07:10.180
But ya learned, right?

07:10.180 --> 07:12.098
It w-won't happen again.

07:12.223 --> 07:13.433
Good.

07:13.433 --> 07:15.352
'Cause I need your head
in the game. [sniffs]

07:15.352 --> 07:17.062
You're driving me
and Sofia tonight.

07:17.187 --> 07:18.480
I'm-I'm-I'm...

07:19.856 --> 07:21.274
driving both of you?

07:21.399 --> 07:23.568
Yeah. Whaddaya think
the new clothes are for?

07:23.693 --> 07:26.154
You're my guy. Can't have you
lookin' like a schmuck.

07:27.364 --> 07:28.323
[sighs]

07:29.741 --> 07:31.242
Listen, I'm askin' a lot of you.

07:32.243 --> 07:34.996
I get it,
and it just occurred to me

07:34.996 --> 07:36.748
we never discussed your salary.

07:37.582 --> 07:38.792
So...

07:39.376 --> 07:42.462
[Oz counting softly]

07:42.587 --> 07:44.089
Boom, there it is.

07:44.923 --> 07:48.593
What do you say
we start you on one a week, huh?

07:48.718 --> 07:50.470
O-One thousand a week?

07:51.262 --> 07:52.180
Are you serious?

07:53.390 --> 07:55.725
And from now on, you want
something, you ask for it.

07:55.725 --> 07:58.728
How's anyone supposed know your
worth unless you tell 'em, huh?

07:58.728 --> 08:00.772
- I want two thousand.
- [laughs]

08:02.148 --> 08:04.025
- That's what I'm talking about.
- [buzzer sounds]

08:04.025 --> 08:05.860
But no. There she is.

08:08.446 --> 08:10.782
[buzzer sounds]

08:10.907 --> 08:12.826
[phone vibrates]

08:12.826 --> 08:14.536
Fuck, Blackgate.

08:14.536 --> 08:17.122
Gotta be Sal.
I need to take this.

08:17.914 --> 08:19.124
[Oz sighs]

08:19.249 --> 08:21.418
- Kid, buy me some time.
- Hold on, Oz.

08:21.418 --> 08:24.087
What if she asks about
her brother? Or Castillo?

08:24.087 --> 08:25.839
Tell her you had a hand
in killing 'em both.

08:25.964 --> 08:27.298
See what happens.

08:27.924 --> 08:29.467
I'm fucking with you.
She's a pussycat.

08:29.592 --> 08:31.177
She is the Hangman.

08:31.177 --> 08:33.805
Don't believe everything
you read in the papers.

08:33.930 --> 08:35.515
- Hey, Sal.
- [knock at door]

08:35.515 --> 08:38.476
Man of the hour,
I was just thinkin' about you...

08:39.102 --> 08:41.021
[exhales]

08:42.022 --> 08:44.899
Did Nadia tell ya about
that shit I got on Johnny Viti?

08:44.899 --> 08:46.776
Yeah, I'm tryin' to set
something up,

08:46.776 --> 08:48.695
- but the Family's on lockdown.
- [knocking]

08:48.820 --> 08:50.655
[thunder rumbling]

08:53.199 --> 08:54.534
[whispers] Shit.

08:56.202 --> 08:57.912
[breathes deeply]

09:03.835 --> 09:05.628
- Where's Oz?
- He's, uh...

09:05.628 --> 09:08.048
He's just-- He's getting
dressed right now.

09:08.173 --> 09:09.007
Yup.

09:10.508 --> 09:11.384
Welcome.

09:21.978 --> 09:23.355
[smacks lips]

09:24.022 --> 09:25.732
That's, uh...
That's the remote for...

09:25.857 --> 09:27.817
[romantic guitar music
strikes up]

09:27.817 --> 09:29.027
[Victor] Yeah.

09:30.236 --> 09:31.738
- [music stops]
- Tacky.

09:33.365 --> 09:36.451
Would you, uh--
Do you wanna, uh, s-sit down?

09:36.451 --> 09:37.786
I'd rather not.

09:43.249 --> 09:45.043
So, where'd Oz find you?

09:46.878 --> 09:48.254
I, uh...

09:48.254 --> 09:50.965
did some, uh, work.

09:50.965 --> 09:54.761
I, um, worked
on one of his cars.

09:54.886 --> 09:56.262
I mean, I worked on his car.

09:56.262 --> 10:00.725
He thought that I-I did...
uh, good,

10:00.850 --> 10:03.395
and so he... hired me

10:03.520 --> 10:04.646
as his driver.

10:05.355 --> 10:06.648
You're a mechanic?

10:07.232 --> 10:10.485
Um, yeah. Uh, kind of, yes.

10:10.485 --> 10:13.238
I, uh... I sort of...

10:15.782 --> 10:18.410
- [lighter clicking]
- Um...

10:19.536 --> 10:21.746
Then why can't you
work a lighter?

10:22.372 --> 10:23.832
I think this thing's
broken actually.

10:33.258 --> 10:34.342
That's good.

10:37.637 --> 10:38.680
What's your name?

10:39.389 --> 10:41.933
It's Vi... uh, Victor.

10:42.892 --> 10:43.977
[Victor sighs]

10:44.102 --> 10:46.855
Victor, the young mechanic.

10:48.565 --> 10:51.026
Oz used to be my driver.
Did he tell you that?

10:53.778 --> 10:54.863
I didn't think so.

10:56.322 --> 10:57.615
[door creaks]

10:58.450 --> 10:59.451
There she is.

11:00.410 --> 11:02.454
- What'd I miss?
- I like your place.

11:03.121 --> 11:04.122
Thank you.

11:04.998 --> 11:06.124
Understated.

11:08.668 --> 11:10.378
Let's go. [clears throat]

11:13.131 --> 11:14.799
- [Oz] Hey, ready?
- [Victor] Mm-hmm.

11:16.760 --> 11:17.635
Just us.

11:18.636 --> 11:20.638
Sorry, Victor.
It's gonna be a long night.

11:21.639 --> 11:23.308
I thought we was just
picking up a shipment.

11:23.433 --> 11:25.185
It's something like that.

11:25.185 --> 11:26.353
[Oz sniffs]

11:27.854 --> 11:28.897
[Sofia] Come on.

11:28.897 --> 11:30.148
You're driving.

11:30.607 --> 11:31.900
Just like old times.

11:35.195 --> 11:36.738
- Stay put.
- [door opens]

11:40.325 --> 11:42.160
You do anything stupid,
I'll sense it.

11:50.460 --> 11:52.754
[line ringing]

11:56.508 --> 11:57.467
[Graciela] Victor?

11:57.467 --> 11:59.094
- Hi.
- Where've you been?

11:59.094 --> 12:00.762
[siren wailing]

12:00.762 --> 12:03.348
[train clattering]

12:12.857 --> 12:14.442
[men chattering]

12:19.864 --> 12:21.032
Always a gentleman.

12:23.868 --> 12:25.203
Wanna tell me
what's going on here?

12:26.204 --> 12:27.831
I thought Alberto
told you everything.

12:27.831 --> 12:30.667
Well, Al wasn't exactly a
detail-oriented guy, you know?

12:30.667 --> 12:32.961
- Marco.
- He told me he had big plans

12:32.961 --> 12:34.713
and he needed my help
with distro.

12:36.339 --> 12:37.966
[man] How many more we got left?

12:38.842 --> 12:39.801
[Sofia] As promised.

12:40.552 --> 12:42.929
Perfect clarity. Untraceable.

12:44.014 --> 12:45.098
[ominous music playing]

12:45.223 --> 12:46.433
[Marco] Looks good, Ms. Falcone.

12:47.017 --> 12:48.351
[cart rattling]

12:48.351 --> 12:49.894
[zipping]

12:52.272 --> 12:53.398
- This it?
- We got more.

12:53.523 --> 12:54.941
Sorry about your brother.

12:55.066 --> 12:56.443
Tell your men to be careful.

12:57.694 --> 12:58.820
[man] Come on, let's go.

12:58.820 --> 12:59.779
Hey.

13:01.573 --> 13:03.950
This shit... came from Arkham?

13:05.076 --> 13:07.162
I thought this was all
Al's plan.

13:08.872 --> 13:09.998
I know you did.

13:13.376 --> 13:15.920
[upbeat rock music
playing over speakers]

13:19.549 --> 13:22.010
Oz, meet Trey Bloom.
Our chemist.

13:24.054 --> 13:25.305
Welcome, brother.

13:29.934 --> 13:31.811
The fuck you cookin' in here?

13:34.272 --> 13:35.273
[Sofia] This way.

13:40.153 --> 13:41.529
[Trey] Gorgeous product.

13:41.529 --> 13:44.032
This substrate is making
them fruit like wildfire.

13:44.032 --> 13:45.283
[door clangs shut]

13:47.494 --> 13:49.162
[sprinklers hissing]

13:51.456 --> 13:52.707
Mushrooms?

13:55.794 --> 13:56.878
[Sofia] Don't!

13:58.171 --> 13:59.631
They're extremely fragile.

14:00.465 --> 14:02.258
[Trey] Any change in
the moisture or temperature

14:02.258 --> 14:03.927
could wipe out
the entire colony.

14:03.927 --> 14:05.553
Oh yeah? The whole colony, huh?

14:05.553 --> 14:07.847
Fuckin' great. Hey, listen.

14:08.473 --> 14:09.974
I know you been gone a while.

14:10.809 --> 14:13.186
You can buy shrooms
in any dorm room in Gotham.

14:13.687 --> 14:16.981
It's not exactly what I'd call,
uh, revolutionary.

14:18.608 --> 14:20.694
You have
a very limited imagination.

14:20.694 --> 14:22.821
[intriguing music playing]

14:22.946 --> 14:23.988
Come here.

14:29.953 --> 14:31.663
It's not the mushrooms
that we're using.

14:32.956 --> 14:34.708
[Trey] They're
the basidiospores.

14:35.709 --> 14:36.835
The fuck d'you just say to me?

14:37.460 --> 14:41.006
These are bleeding tooth fungi,
a rare strain.

14:41.131 --> 14:43.174
The psychoactive
compound in the sap

14:43.299 --> 14:45.844
creates a potent,
euphoric stimulant.

14:45.969 --> 14:47.429
It's a completely
different high.

14:49.723 --> 14:51.057
So it's a party drug.

14:51.725 --> 14:52.600
[Sofia chuckles]

14:53.977 --> 14:54.936
Sure.

14:54.936 --> 14:56.021
I suppose.

14:58.189 --> 15:00.859
And you took this shit
in Arkham?

15:03.236 --> 15:04.696
We have a small
test batch ready,

15:04.821 --> 15:06.156
and, um, after tonight,

15:06.156 --> 15:09.159
we're going to have
a hell of a lot more.

15:09.159 --> 15:12.162
Sure, but you can't use your
Family's connects on this.

15:12.162 --> 15:14.748
You know,
not without Luca gettin' wind.

15:15.665 --> 15:16.791
That's why you're here.

15:17.375 --> 15:19.044
You seem to know
everybody's business.

15:19.586 --> 15:21.463
So, now's your time
to shine, Oz.

15:22.839 --> 15:24.632
Find me a distributor
and we'll paint the town red.

15:27.427 --> 15:28.303
[knock at door]

15:35.685 --> 15:36.895
- Hey.
- Hi.

15:37.020 --> 15:38.021
I'm sorry I didn't call--

15:38.021 --> 15:39.731
I'm just glad you're safe.

15:41.399 --> 15:43.109
[mellow R & B music
playing on stereo]

15:44.611 --> 15:47.447
- Calvin's not with you, is he?
- [bottle cap pops]

15:47.447 --> 15:49.491
He disappeared
around the same time you did.

15:49.491 --> 15:52.577
- I thought maybe...
- Uh... no, no.

15:52.702 --> 15:54.162
I-I haven't seen him.

15:55.246 --> 15:56.247
Thanks.

16:00.043 --> 16:02.253
So, you just drive
this club owner around,

16:02.379 --> 16:04.255
- and he lets you stay here?
- [chuckles]

16:05.131 --> 16:07.133
Uh, pretty much, yeah.

16:07.133 --> 16:08.802
[both laugh]

16:08.802 --> 16:10.512
Um, shit, sorry.

16:10.512 --> 16:11.721
- Hang on...
- [Graciela laughs]

16:11.721 --> 16:14.683
I-I... It's, um... you know.

16:14.683 --> 16:16.601
- It's okay, I get it.
- Okay.

16:16.726 --> 16:17.936
- Good.
- [laughs]

16:19.062 --> 16:20.647
Yo, this place is bougie.

16:21.439 --> 16:23.108
- [Victor chuckles]
- It is.

16:24.651 --> 16:25.777
And you are too now.

16:25.902 --> 16:28.113
- I'm bougie?
- Mm-mmm. [laughs]

16:32.492 --> 16:33.785
You look good.

16:34.994 --> 16:36.287
I missed you.

16:40.834 --> 16:42.293
I'm leaving, Victor.

16:43.795 --> 16:45.672
I'm going to California.

16:45.797 --> 16:46.798
[stammers] Wh...

16:47.632 --> 16:48.675
Why?

16:48.800 --> 16:51.678
Why-Why... would you do that?

16:52.846 --> 16:54.431
'Cause our school is underwater

16:54.431 --> 16:57.183
and I don't wanna live
in a FEMA camp anymore.

16:57.976 --> 16:59.477
Yeah, but your-- you...

17:00.353 --> 17:01.479
I mean...

17:02.480 --> 17:05.525
your-your-your life is here.

17:06.818 --> 17:08.153
Not anymore.

17:11.114 --> 17:12.574
Our families are dead.

17:14.659 --> 17:16.661
We gotta take care
of ourselves now.

17:17.829 --> 17:18.872
When?

17:20.165 --> 17:23.335
When-When are you going?

17:24.461 --> 17:25.837
Tomorrow night.

17:26.546 --> 17:28.923
- Alright.
- I'm taking a bus out.

17:29.549 --> 17:30.592
[Victor murmurs]

17:34.220 --> 17:35.722
You hungry? I...

17:35.847 --> 17:37.015
I got us, uh...

17:38.183 --> 17:40.685
pizza if you want a--
if you want a slice.

17:44.022 --> 17:45.190
[Graciela] Victor.

17:47.067 --> 17:48.193
Hey.

17:50.028 --> 17:51.738
You've got a good thing
going here.

17:51.863 --> 17:53.531
I'm really happy for you.

17:54.657 --> 17:55.700
'Cause, like...

17:56.826 --> 17:58.787
this is what you want. Right?

18:01.915 --> 18:03.249
[inhales sharply]

18:04.542 --> 18:05.543
'Cause...

18:06.544 --> 18:08.713
you-you could come with me.

18:10.507 --> 18:12.050
We could start over.

18:12.884 --> 18:14.010
Really?

18:14.010 --> 18:15.095
Yeah.

18:20.433 --> 18:21.643
I don't-- I don't...

18:22.560 --> 18:23.770
I don't, uh...

18:24.354 --> 18:25.647
I'm not sure that...

18:26.272 --> 18:27.691
[sighs]

18:27.691 --> 18:29.234
I'm not sure
that he'd let me go.

18:29.901 --> 18:31.236
Who? Your boss?

18:33.279 --> 18:34.447
Why would he care?

18:34.447 --> 18:35.573
[Victor sighs]

18:38.201 --> 18:40.829
He's not just like a...
a club owner.

18:40.829 --> 18:41.830
He's, um...

18:46.710 --> 18:48.169
He's like a gangster.

18:49.963 --> 18:50.839
Oh.

18:51.715 --> 18:54.259
If I took off,
I don't think that, um...

18:55.719 --> 18:57.262
It's weird, it's like, uh...

18:58.638 --> 19:00.682
He kind of likes
having me around.

19:01.599 --> 19:03.476
He's kinda... he's kinda lonely.

19:04.936 --> 19:06.688
And I've seen stuff.

19:06.688 --> 19:08.857
You know, stuff
that I-I shouldn't have,

19:08.857 --> 19:11.609
so if left, I don't know

19:12.736 --> 19:14.279
what he would do.

19:14.404 --> 19:17.949
Then... you definitely
shouldn't stay.

19:20.493 --> 19:21.911
I mean,
nothing good can come

19:21.911 --> 19:23.663
from working
for a guy like that.

19:25.248 --> 19:26.624
That is not who you are.

19:31.629 --> 19:33.006
You sound like my dad.

19:35.508 --> 19:36.551
Sorry.

19:36.551 --> 19:37.886
No, no.

19:40.263 --> 19:41.389
It's not a bad thing.

19:43.433 --> 19:44.351
[phone buzzing]

19:44.476 --> 19:45.352
Oh, no.

19:45.477 --> 19:48.188
Um... Shit.

19:48.313 --> 19:50.065
Uh, he...

19:50.065 --> 19:51.900
He's on his way back,
so you gotta go.

19:51.900 --> 19:53.193
- What?
- Yeah.

19:53.985 --> 19:55.070
Wait.

19:55.070 --> 19:56.363
Um...

19:57.530 --> 19:59.199
- Here. Take this.
- Whoa, that's--

19:59.199 --> 20:00.492
No, no, listen.

20:02.202 --> 20:03.578
Stay somewhere nice.

20:04.954 --> 20:06.790
- And get me a ticket.
- Really?

20:06.790 --> 20:08.958
Yeah. I'm gonna meet you
at Gotham Station.

20:08.958 --> 20:10.085
- Okay.
- Okay.

20:10.085 --> 20:12.253
Are you gonna tell
your boss, or...?

20:12.253 --> 20:13.880
I'm gonna figure that out.

20:14.005 --> 20:16.424
[soft music playing]

20:24.891 --> 20:26.309
- Okay.
- Okay.

20:26.309 --> 20:27.727
- I'll text you.
- Okay.

20:27.852 --> 20:29.521
- Okay.
- Alright.

20:31.064 --> 20:33.066
[breathing rapidly]

20:33.191 --> 20:34.901
[insects chirring]

20:44.536 --> 20:45.704
[Viti] Sofia.

20:51.042 --> 20:52.377
Where you been?

20:52.502 --> 20:53.753
What's with all the muscle?

20:54.337 --> 20:55.630
And all the cars outside?

20:55.630 --> 20:58.174
We all gotta lay low
until shit dies down.

20:58.174 --> 20:59.426
That's your grand plan?

20:59.426 --> 21:01.219
Our men are being gunned down

21:01.344 --> 21:03.430
by the Maronis
in broad daylight, but...

21:04.931 --> 21:06.683
you're throwing
a fuckin' sleepover.

21:07.392 --> 21:09.436
This business
ain't your business.

21:10.020 --> 21:11.479
Take a fuckin' hint.

21:12.355 --> 21:15.275
Luca, he's the head
of the Family now.

21:16.401 --> 21:19.571
Okay? So, when he tells you
to go to Italy,

21:20.238 --> 21:21.781
you get on a fucking plane.

21:27.245 --> 21:29.205
Did you print this out yourself?

21:29.205 --> 21:30.248
[scoffs]

21:30.915 --> 21:32.751
Look, honey,

21:33.585 --> 21:35.170
I know you're not right
in the head.

21:35.170 --> 21:36.921
I mean, that's
pretty damn clear.

21:38.381 --> 21:39.924
But I'm not scared of you.

21:41.885 --> 21:44.637
All I see is a spoiled brat
who got what she deserved.

21:48.933 --> 21:50.143
[inhales]

21:51.227 --> 21:52.437
[sighs] Thank you.

21:52.562 --> 21:54.689
[paper crumples]

21:55.440 --> 21:56.775
I appreciate this.

21:58.735 --> 22:00.779
- I just need some time to get--
- Two days.

22:02.280 --> 22:03.448
Then you go to Italy.

22:07.077 --> 22:09.037
Or I tell people
that's where you went.

22:14.626 --> 22:17.045
[car horns honking]

22:17.045 --> 22:20.507
[loud traffic humming]

22:20.507 --> 22:22.384
[hip-hop music plays,
then stops]

22:22.384 --> 22:23.802
[Oz] Vic, grab the case.

22:26.137 --> 22:27.138
Chop chop!

22:28.848 --> 22:29.766
[car door shuts]

22:29.766 --> 22:31.893
[hip-hop music plays nearby]

22:33.311 --> 22:34.479
[Sofia] Chinatown, huh?

22:37.607 --> 22:40.026
You're aware my father pushed
the Triads out of the drug game?

22:40.151 --> 22:41.319
Yeah, I was there, doll.

22:41.611 --> 22:43.279
But we need someone
who ain't gonna rat us out

22:43.279 --> 22:45.031
as soon as we tell 'em
our plan, you know?

22:45.156 --> 22:46.533
Come on. There it is.

22:46.658 --> 22:47.826
[bottles clinking]

22:47.951 --> 22:49.119
What's all this?

22:49.119 --> 22:51.538
Little hospitality gift
for my pal Link Tsai.

22:51.538 --> 22:53.456
A Triad deputy
who runs their clubs.

22:53.456 --> 22:54.791
We're friendly.

22:54.791 --> 22:56.835
Why are we wasting our time
with a deputy?

22:57.752 --> 22:59.546
Feng Zhao is the Dai Lo,

22:59.546 --> 23:01.506
the only person that can
authorize a partnership.

23:01.631 --> 23:03.758
We don't got a relationship
with Feng Zhao, do we?

23:04.509 --> 23:06.052
You got me, I got Link.

23:06.511 --> 23:08.054
Kid, keep your eye on the bag.

23:08.638 --> 23:10.598
- [hip-hop playing on stereo]
- [Oz] Hey.

23:10.598 --> 23:11.850
[man] We're closed.

23:11.975 --> 23:13.393
[men speaking Mandarin]

23:13.518 --> 23:14.561
[Oz] How ya doin'?

23:15.186 --> 23:16.229
I'm Oz.

23:16.855 --> 23:18.606
We're here to see Link Tsai.

23:20.358 --> 23:21.526
[Oz clears his throat]

23:24.404 --> 23:25.447
There you go.

23:25.447 --> 23:26.698
Got it?

23:31.494 --> 23:32.746
It's in the back.

23:36.708 --> 23:37.959
Didn't know you were carrying.

23:37.959 --> 23:39.586
Well, I figured you were, so...

23:39.711 --> 23:41.212
Oh, this is unreal.

23:42.672 --> 23:43.882
Maybe next time, call ahead.

23:44.007 --> 23:46.009
Sometimes it's better
to ask for forgiveness.

23:46.009 --> 23:48.094
I told you not to show your face
till you had my money.

23:48.094 --> 23:51.264
Link, brought you some top-shelf
from the 44.

23:51.389 --> 23:52.390
My best shit.

23:53.391 --> 23:54.476
You think I give a fuck?

23:55.060 --> 23:56.978
I sent you a whole truck
of cigarettes.

23:57.854 --> 23:58.855
Where's my cut?

23:58.855 --> 24:00.774
You think I'd come here
empty-handed?

24:00.774 --> 24:03.151
Come on, we both know that
if I ever truly left you hangin'

24:03.151 --> 24:05.070
there'd be a bullet
between my eyes.

24:05.195 --> 24:07.447
I got a real opportunity
for you here,

24:07.447 --> 24:10.325
but it's kinda hard to focus
with a gun pointed at my face.

24:13.870 --> 24:14.996
[in Mandarin]

24:19.292 --> 24:20.585
[in English] Sofia Falcone.

24:21.252 --> 24:23.546
We've never met,
but I know who you are.

24:23.546 --> 24:24.756
Good for you.

24:27.592 --> 24:30.428
This... is why we're here.

24:30.553 --> 24:31.429
[Oz] We're calling it...

24:32.972 --> 24:33.932
Bliss.

24:40.730 --> 24:42.857
[indistinct chatter
in background]

24:44.109 --> 24:46.027
[Victor] Hey, Oz... [sighs]

24:46.945 --> 24:48.029
So...

24:49.239 --> 24:51.616
there's this girl, and, uh...

24:52.117 --> 24:54.619
she means a lot to me.

24:55.453 --> 24:56.955
And-And you do too.

24:57.789 --> 24:59.666
You know I'm not a rat. Right?

24:59.791 --> 25:01.167
You know I'd never...

25:01.167 --> 25:04.379
If I... If I ever saw
anything...

25:05.630 --> 25:07.173
I would never say anything...

25:11.594 --> 25:12.971
He's gonna kill me.

25:13.471 --> 25:14.806
He's gonna kill me.

25:19.811 --> 25:21.396
[brakes squealing]

25:21.396 --> 25:23.565
[indistinct radio chatter]

25:23.565 --> 25:24.733
[siren chirps]

25:25.442 --> 25:26.484
[Victor] Shit.

25:28.653 --> 25:29.487
[car door shuts]

25:30.697 --> 25:32.323
[breathing rapidly]

25:33.116 --> 25:33.992
[inhales sharply]

25:34.117 --> 25:36.077
[tense music playing]

25:39.539 --> 25:40.874
[knocking loudly]

25:45.837 --> 25:47.505
[policeman]
Step out of the car, son.

25:52.010 --> 25:53.261
What, uh...

25:53.261 --> 25:55.263
W-W... Um...

25:56.556 --> 25:59.392
Wha... W-What did I do?

25:59.517 --> 26:00.518
You nervous?

26:00.643 --> 26:02.020
No, I just-just, um...

26:02.145 --> 26:03.980
I-I s-- uh...

26:03.980 --> 26:06.483
s-s-stutter sometimes.

26:06.483 --> 26:08.401
You're idling in a loading zone.
Turn around.

26:09.319 --> 26:11.071
- I can just move the--
- Turn around.

26:11.071 --> 26:12.280
Hands on the hood.

26:12.739 --> 26:13.740
Uh...

26:15.992 --> 26:17.369
[policeman] Is this your car?

26:18.078 --> 26:20.455
- It's my boss's car.
- Pretty flashy.

26:25.418 --> 26:27.462
That's a lot of money for a kid
to be carrying around.

26:35.095 --> 26:36.971
I don't know w-what
you're talking about.

26:36.971 --> 26:38.556
I don't have any money.

26:38.682 --> 26:39.724
[music fades]

26:41.726 --> 26:42.727
Guess not.

26:45.063 --> 26:47.565
Soon as your boss is back,
get outta here.

26:50.026 --> 26:51.903
[receding footsteps]

26:53.738 --> 26:55.323
[Link] No fucking way.

26:56.700 --> 26:59.744
You seriously trying
to sell me on a... a coup?

26:59.869 --> 27:03.623
The two of you are gonna
take over the Falcone Family

27:03.748 --> 27:04.958
in the middle of a gang war?

27:05.083 --> 27:06.209
A coup?

27:06.209 --> 27:07.836
[chuckles]

27:07.836 --> 27:09.754
What are you, readin' books
or something?

27:10.422 --> 27:13.299
No, what we got goin' is
more of a corporate restructure.

27:13.425 --> 27:14.342
[Sofia] Mm-hmm.

27:16.553 --> 27:18.263
And we ain't goin' at it alone.

27:19.389 --> 27:22.350
We got support
from within the Family.

27:23.476 --> 27:24.769
- You do?
- 'Course.

27:24.894 --> 27:26.730
You think we'd walk in
without our shit on lock?

27:26.730 --> 27:27.814
Come on.

27:27.939 --> 27:28.857
[Link] Who?

27:30.400 --> 27:32.444
- Who?
- [Link] Yeah, who?

27:37.115 --> 27:37.991
Johnny Viti.

27:38.116 --> 27:40.660
[dishes clinking in background]

27:41.327 --> 27:43.455
- That's bullshit.
- [Oz] Fuck you, bullshit.

27:43.580 --> 27:46.041
Luca Falcone's underboss
is backing you?

27:46.041 --> 27:47.459
He's backing me.

27:48.460 --> 27:50.003
Johnny is my mother's cousin.

27:50.587 --> 27:52.297
He and I are very close.

27:52.839 --> 27:56.134
He also knows that Bliss
is a game changer.

27:56.259 --> 27:58.803
- [Oz] Uh-huh.
- And that Luca...

27:59.304 --> 28:00.764
doesn't have the balls
to see it through.

28:00.764 --> 28:02.057
That's true.

28:02.057 --> 28:05.477
Look how he mishandled
our Drops operation.

28:05.602 --> 28:07.187
- Disaster.
- Embarrassing.

28:07.187 --> 28:10.273
- [Oz] Yeah, that's right.
- Zhao's gonna need proof.

28:10.273 --> 28:12.942
What does he want,
a letter of recommendation?

28:12.942 --> 28:14.402
A phone call would suffice.

28:14.986 --> 28:17.655
From Johnny Viti, directly.

28:18.823 --> 28:20.492
Or are you full of shit
as usual, Oz?

28:20.617 --> 28:21.910
Nah, my word's good.

28:23.328 --> 28:25.246
But since your face
don't seem to agree...

28:25.246 --> 28:26.414
[scoffs]

28:27.332 --> 28:29.334
...I'll have Viti give
the old man a ring,

28:29.459 --> 28:30.794
let him know
we're all pals here.

28:30.794 --> 28:32.754
And once he does,
you're gonna get us

28:32.754 --> 28:34.464
an audience with Mr. Zhao.

28:34.464 --> 28:36.007
And you're gonna do it tonight.

28:36.132 --> 28:37.300
Right here.

28:37.300 --> 28:39.135
We'll set up a trial run
for the drug.

28:39.135 --> 28:41.388
[Oz] And when it all goes off
without a hitch,

28:41.388 --> 28:44.099
we'll, uh, you know,
get you a fair price.

28:44.099 --> 28:45.350
That's right.

28:47.310 --> 28:50.188
I always knew it was a matter of
time before you made a move, Oz.

28:51.856 --> 28:53.233
Didn't think it would
come like this.

28:55.151 --> 28:57.195
Assuming that you hold up
your end,

28:59.030 --> 29:00.907
I'll get you a sit-down
with the Dai Lo.

29:03.034 --> 29:04.035
After that,

29:05.829 --> 29:06.746
it's outta my hands.

29:08.540 --> 29:09.499
[Link clears his throat]

29:09.499 --> 29:11.376
[receding footsteps]

29:13.169 --> 29:14.379
[whispers] There it is.

29:15.505 --> 29:18.717
What aren't you telling me
about Johnny Viti?

29:19.592 --> 29:21.761
Look at you.
You're havin' fun, I can tell.

29:21.886 --> 29:23.888
- Oz. I don't-- Oz.
- [chuckles]

29:24.014 --> 29:26.349
Alright, listen. Jesus.
I got a plan.

29:26.349 --> 29:28.810
Okay? You're just gonna
have to trust me.

29:28.810 --> 29:30.770
[tense music playing]

29:33.857 --> 29:34.858
[music fades]

29:35.734 --> 29:37.277
[laughs] You musta
pissed yourself.

29:37.402 --> 29:39.029
So then what?
Cop finds your money...?

29:39.029 --> 29:42.991
Right, so he-he finds my money
and I said, uh...

29:42.991 --> 29:46.953
I said... I go,
"I don't have any money."

29:47.579 --> 29:49.873
And he just took it.

29:49.873 --> 29:51.833
- He took the whole fuckin' G?
- [chuckles]

29:51.833 --> 29:54.210
[laughs] The motherfucker!

29:54.210 --> 29:56.963
Well, that's the cost
of doin' business, kid.

29:57.088 --> 29:58.506
Welcome to the life!

30:00.258 --> 30:04.220
[women chattering indistinctly]

30:04.220 --> 30:06.598
[light chamber music playing]

30:12.562 --> 30:14.064
- So, Oz--
- Have we made any decisions?

30:14.064 --> 30:15.940
I'll take the coq au vin.
Do that again.

30:16.066 --> 30:17.901
- Vic?
- Uh, right.

30:17.901 --> 30:22.864
I'll do the, uh, the-the steak
f-- um... [stutters]

30:22.864 --> 30:26.368
Um, the steak, uh... f...

30:28.411 --> 30:29.621
Steak f-f--

30:29.746 --> 30:31.414
- [waiter] Steak frites.
- Hey.

30:31.414 --> 30:32.791
Don't do that.

30:32.916 --> 30:34.959
The man was speakin'.
Let him finish.

30:35.919 --> 30:37.087
I apologize.

30:37.087 --> 30:38.338
Please.

30:38.463 --> 30:39.798
Yeah, no, the, uh...

30:42.634 --> 30:43.718
steak f...

30:44.302 --> 30:45.136
Uh...

30:46.513 --> 30:48.306
...frites.
Steak frites, thanks.

30:49.265 --> 30:50.350
Right away, sir.

30:52.977 --> 30:55.063
"Sir."
He's trying to save his tip.

30:55.063 --> 30:56.815
You know, you don't
got to do that.

30:56.940 --> 30:58.817
Yeah, I know. You should do it.

30:59.651 --> 31:01.069
Fuck what they think.

31:01.069 --> 31:02.404
Let 'em wait.

31:02.404 --> 31:04.447
You know, take up space.

31:04.447 --> 31:05.615
You got fight in you, Vic.

31:05.615 --> 31:07.325
You gotta let it out.

31:11.955 --> 31:13.164
What did your, uh...

31:15.166 --> 31:16.501
What'd your parents do?

31:17.460 --> 31:18.920
What line of work were they in?

31:21.840 --> 31:23.341
Well, my mom,

31:24.676 --> 31:27.887
she was a, uh...
a home health aide.

31:28.013 --> 31:29.514
- Yeah?
- And, uh...

31:30.348 --> 31:32.684
my dad, he was a mechanic.

31:32.809 --> 31:33.768
Oh, okay.

31:33.768 --> 31:36.604
But in... in his heart,

31:37.230 --> 31:38.898
- the man was a chef.
- Chef?

31:38.898 --> 31:40.400
[laughs] Yeah, loved to cook.

31:40.400 --> 31:41.693
- Is that right?
- Yeah.

31:41.818 --> 31:43.820
It was mostly, um,

31:43.820 --> 31:45.864
- M-Mexican and Dominican stuff.
- [Oz] Yeah, yeah.

31:45.989 --> 31:48.867
Like carnitas and sancocho...

31:48.992 --> 31:50.368
- [chuckles] Beautiful.
- Things like that.

31:50.493 --> 31:53.329
Yeah, yeah.
Um... But, man, I mean,

31:53.329 --> 31:55.707
he would've got
a kick out of this place too.

31:55.832 --> 31:59.836
The-The s-snails
and-and the oysters...

31:59.836 --> 32:02.380
You know, it's, uh... it's nice.

32:02.505 --> 32:04.215
And I-I don't think...

32:04.341 --> 32:06.843
I don't think he ever got
to eat in a lot of

32:06.843 --> 32:08.595
n-nice restaurants.

32:11.014 --> 32:12.223
That ain't right.

32:13.391 --> 32:14.976
That ain't fucking right.

32:17.103 --> 32:19.731
Look... Fuck.

32:19.856 --> 32:22.275
The world ain't set up
for the honest man to succeed.

32:23.193 --> 32:24.486
Mechanic's a good job.

32:24.486 --> 32:26.488
That should be the
American dream right there.

32:26.488 --> 32:28.948
You know, a beautiful story
with a happy ending.

32:31.034 --> 32:33.411
But that ain't the way
the world works, Vic.

32:35.246 --> 32:36.414
America's a hustle.

32:39.876 --> 32:41.127
What was his name?

32:41.127 --> 32:43.421
[somber music playing]

32:44.547 --> 32:45.674
Juan.

32:47.801 --> 32:49.302
Juan Ramon Aguilar.

32:50.887 --> 32:54.099
To Juan Ramon Aguilar.

32:57.435 --> 32:58.770
He raised a good son.

33:03.817 --> 33:05.610
Your dad would be
proud of you, Vic.

33:13.451 --> 33:15.453
[ominous music playing]

33:16.454 --> 33:17.956
[softly] All right.
It's go time.

33:27.799 --> 33:29.050
Hiya, Tina.

33:29.634 --> 33:31.886
Oz. What are you doing here?

33:31.886 --> 33:33.179
I need a favor.

33:34.681 --> 33:35.807
It's gonna sting.

33:36.474 --> 33:38.643
[tense, dramatic music playing]

33:41.104 --> 33:42.313
[bell dings]

33:43.982 --> 33:45.525
[Oz] Took ya long enough.

33:45.525 --> 33:47.861
- Afraid he'll finish early?
- [Oz laughs]

33:51.322 --> 33:52.240
[lock beeps]

33:54.659 --> 33:57.162
[moaning]

33:57.287 --> 33:58.663
[Oz] Congratulations
on the nuptials.

34:00.123 --> 34:01.750
What the fuck?

34:03.043 --> 34:04.002
Get out.

34:05.337 --> 34:07.172
[Oz] How's the fuckin' going,
Johnny?

34:08.965 --> 34:10.133
[Sofia] Tina.

34:10.133 --> 34:11.760
Don't forget your panties.

34:15.513 --> 34:17.974
- [door opens, closes]
- [Oz chuckles]

34:17.974 --> 34:19.517
One word about this to Luca,
I swear--

34:19.642 --> 34:21.686
And what, Johnny?
What're you gonna do?

34:21.811 --> 34:24.064
- Your ghost will haunt me?
- [Sofia chuckles]

34:24.064 --> 34:25.899
I gotta say,
fuckin' the Boss's wife?

34:26.024 --> 34:27.484
I mean, that's bush league.

34:27.484 --> 34:30.195
So what? Are you two
working together now?

34:30.737 --> 34:32.072
Oz is working for me.

34:32.864 --> 34:34.240
[Viti] Are you fucking serious?

34:34.240 --> 34:36.284
You're going against Luca
to back a psychopath?

34:36.284 --> 34:38.703
You're gonna back her too, Viti.
That's why we're here.

34:39.412 --> 34:40.663
And I don't think
she appreciates

34:40.663 --> 34:41.748
you calling her a psycho.

34:41.873 --> 34:43.458
He's absolutely right. I don't.

34:43.458 --> 34:45.043
Here's what's gonna happen.

34:47.671 --> 34:51.383
You are gonna get Feng Zhao
on the line.

34:51.508 --> 34:54.219
You're gonna tell him you
sat down with me and Sofia

34:54.344 --> 34:56.054
and that we got your support.

34:56.179 --> 34:57.597
- Sound good?
- Are you fuckin' nuts?

34:57.597 --> 34:59.307
You want me to lie
to the head of the Triads?

34:59.307 --> 35:00.725
Doesn't have to be a lie,

35:00.892 --> 35:02.435
dependin' on which way
you wanna play it.

35:02.894 --> 35:04.771
We could all get rid
of Luca together, right?

35:04.896 --> 35:06.398
- That's right.
- Think about it. I get rich.

35:06.523 --> 35:07.774
Sofia gets the Family.

35:07.899 --> 35:09.150
You get to fuck
Tina's brains out

35:09.150 --> 35:10.610
on a beach with white sand.

35:10.735 --> 35:13.738
- Sounds pretty good.
- Don't it? What do you say?

35:13.863 --> 35:16.741
Sofia, I thought you knew better
than to trust this asshole.

35:17.450 --> 35:18.868
Especially after
what he did to you.

35:18.868 --> 35:20.161
[Oz] What I did to her?

35:20.161 --> 35:21.871
Fuck you--
Shut the fuck up, Johnny.

35:21.871 --> 35:25.583
After you got locked up,
Carmine let him run the 44,

35:26.251 --> 35:27.794
but he never respected him.

35:29.546 --> 35:31.423
And I bet you don't
respect him either, do you?

35:32.465 --> 35:34.384
- Hmm?
- [tense music playing]

35:34.384 --> 35:36.636
You're fun at a card game,
or over drinks.

35:36.636 --> 35:38.888
I'll give you that. But people
don't keep you around

35:38.888 --> 35:40.557
because they think you're smart.

35:40.557 --> 35:42.976
And they sure as shit
don't trust you.

35:43.727 --> 35:44.602
Nah...

35:45.103 --> 35:48.231
People keep the Penguin
around as entertainment,

35:48.231 --> 35:51.067
because everybody knows
you're a goddamn joke.

35:51.067 --> 35:52.736
[Oz] You fuck!

35:52.736 --> 35:53.945
[Viti groans]

35:56.239 --> 35:59.325
This fuckin' funny to you, huh?
You scumbag!

36:00.076 --> 36:03.955
You and the Family,
hangin' Sofia out to dry, huh?

36:05.081 --> 36:08.418
You lowlife,
two-timin' fuckin' coward, Viti.

36:08.418 --> 36:10.128
[tooth cracking]

36:11.171 --> 36:12.047
[grunting]

36:12.047 --> 36:14.758
- [music fades]
- [Viti coughs]

36:14.758 --> 36:17.802
[Viti panting]

36:20.638 --> 36:21.514
Here.

36:24.476 --> 36:26.353
Make the fucking call.

36:26.353 --> 36:30.398
[upbeat electronic dance music
playing]

36:30.398 --> 36:32.317
[people cheering]

36:37.197 --> 36:38.448
Alright, listen up.

36:38.448 --> 36:41.201
Tonight we're bringin'
something new

36:41.201 --> 36:42.994
to the good people of Gotham.

36:43.119 --> 36:45.330
It's a party drug called Bliss.

36:45.955 --> 36:47.874
That's why I asked
you ladies here.

36:47.999 --> 36:49.668
You're the best fuckin'
salespeople I know.

36:49.793 --> 36:52.420
- [all giggling]
- Gonna start at 20 a hit.

36:52.420 --> 36:55.423
Vic here is gonna be our bagman
for the night.

36:55.423 --> 36:57.592
So if any of you ladies
need to re-up,

36:57.592 --> 36:58.551
you go to him.

36:58.677 --> 36:59.803
He'll take your cash,

36:59.803 --> 37:01.846
and I'll get you back
before last call.

37:01.971 --> 37:04.474
- [woman 1] Alright, cool.
- Security knows who you are.

37:04.474 --> 37:06.893
Any trouble, you go straight
to them. Understood?

37:07.644 --> 37:09.562
Get out there and make us
a fuck ton of money.

37:10.855 --> 37:12.774
- Go on, do your thing!
- [woman 2] Let's go, girls!

37:12.774 --> 37:14.109
[woman 3] We on it, baby!

37:14.109 --> 37:15.610
[woman laughs]

37:18.697 --> 37:20.156
[Oz] Hey, kid.

37:20.156 --> 37:22.742
Remember, alright?
They want what you got.

37:22.742 --> 37:24.160
Not the other way around.

37:24.160 --> 37:26.621
Shoulders back.
Take up space, okay?

37:27.747 --> 37:29.082
Hey, hey, hey.

37:29.207 --> 37:30.583
Kid...

37:30.709 --> 37:32.502
I wouldn't ask you to do this

37:32.502 --> 37:34.379
if I didn't know
you could handle it.

37:36.172 --> 37:37.465
I believe in you, kid.

37:38.758 --> 37:40.218
- Got it?
- Mm-hmm.

37:41.177 --> 37:42.387
Get outta here.

37:45.515 --> 37:47.267
- Where you going?
- Powder my nose.

37:47.392 --> 37:48.476
[Oz] Yeah?

37:48.476 --> 37:50.895
[departing footsteps]

37:51.021 --> 37:53.064
[dance music continues]

37:56.443 --> 37:57.527
Inspiring speech.

37:57.527 --> 37:58.570
Thank you.

37:59.362 --> 38:01.740
- Think it will do the trick?
- [Oz] Fuckin' hope so.

38:02.532 --> 38:05.577
Feng Zhao will be here soon.
Hope he likes what he sees.

38:07.537 --> 38:08.830
We're gonna be untouchable.

38:12.792 --> 38:14.419
I can't tell
who wants this more.

38:15.211 --> 38:16.087
Me or you.

38:18.256 --> 38:19.466
I want this for you.

38:21.259 --> 38:23.636
You say all the right things,
don't you, Oz?

38:25.555 --> 38:27.682
Listen, Zhao's gonna wanna
see that we're serious,

38:27.682 --> 38:28.600
that we're a team.

38:28.725 --> 38:30.018
Was it worth it?

38:30.018 --> 38:31.102
[Oz] What's that?

38:31.728 --> 38:32.937
What you did to me.

38:34.230 --> 38:35.607
Was it worth it?

38:36.274 --> 38:38.360
Did you get everything
that you wanted?

38:39.069 --> 38:42.030
'Cause it seems like you just--
you-you want more.

38:42.030 --> 38:43.448
Who's talkin' here?

38:44.240 --> 38:47.285
You or Johnny Viti? He's got you
eatin' outta his hand--

38:47.410 --> 38:49.162
He didn't say anything
I don't already know.

38:49.287 --> 38:50.455
Come on!

38:50.580 --> 38:52.040
We're so close to gettin'
what you want.

38:52.040 --> 38:53.708
- Let's not--
- I asked you a question.

38:53.708 --> 38:56.252
Jesus!
It's been ten fuckin' years!

38:56.252 --> 38:57.420
I know how long it's been,

38:57.420 --> 38:58.713
and I am not some ignorant kid

38:58.713 --> 39:00.465
you can play with anymore.

39:00.590 --> 39:02.801
- That ain't what I'm--
- Zhao is here to see me.

39:04.427 --> 39:05.804
Not my former driver.

39:08.264 --> 39:09.140
Remember that.

39:10.100 --> 39:12.477
["I Came for the Low"
by ZHU playing]

39:14.604 --> 39:16.606
[people laughing]

39:28.827 --> 39:30.745
[Cin] Hey! Vicky!

39:31.454 --> 39:32.831
I need more.

39:32.956 --> 39:33.998
[Victor] How much?

39:34.457 --> 39:35.500
More!

39:38.962 --> 39:39.879
Here you go.

39:42.841 --> 39:45.885
[electronic dance music
continues]

39:49.556 --> 39:50.932
Got something for you.

39:51.725 --> 39:53.685
For the boys at the table.
[laughs]

39:57.397 --> 39:59.607
Yo, you the man with the shit?

39:59.607 --> 40:02.068
- Yup, that's me.
- [man] It's good shit, man.

40:02.068 --> 40:03.611
We gave your girl 200.

40:04.362 --> 40:05.447
[Victor] Here you go.

40:10.577 --> 40:12.370
[Sofia] There is no
better feeling,

40:12.495 --> 40:13.997
and there's
nothing else like it.

40:13.997 --> 40:16.124
People can see that.
They can feel it.

40:16.666 --> 40:19.044
And that translates
into dollars, Mr. Zhao.

40:19.169 --> 40:21.046
[Oz] We've raised the price
twice already.

40:21.171 --> 40:22.255
It hasn't affected sales.

40:22.756 --> 40:24.507
We're projectin' sixty a hit.

40:24.507 --> 40:26.926
Sixty a fuckin' hit?
On the first night?

40:27.385 --> 40:28.762
It's unheard of.

40:28.762 --> 40:30.263
Imagine the future.

40:30.388 --> 40:33.141
Our drug,
your clubs, your casinos...

40:33.141 --> 40:34.100
You see it?

40:36.853 --> 40:38.396
There's certainly
a lot of potential

40:38.521 --> 40:40.398
to your plan, Ms. Falcone.

40:41.399 --> 40:42.525
I won't deny that.

40:43.526 --> 40:47.072
But even if you have the support
of the underboss,

40:48.406 --> 40:49.908
the risk here is too great.

40:51.076 --> 40:52.744
[sniffs] Why is that?

40:53.703 --> 40:55.955
The Falcones have a history
with the Triads.

40:56.081 --> 40:58.208
- I'm sure you're aware.
- My father pushed you out.

40:58.333 --> 41:00.251
He relegated you to Chinatown.
I know.

41:00.377 --> 41:01.294
[grumbles]

41:01.961 --> 41:05.131
When he died,
I opened a bottle of champagne.

41:05.131 --> 41:08.426
And as soon as I had the chance,
I danced on his grave.

41:09.135 --> 41:11.429
We have more in common
than you might think.

41:11.554 --> 41:12.681
[sighs]

41:13.890 --> 41:15.809
Still... him I knew.

41:16.309 --> 41:17.477
But you...

41:18.978 --> 41:20.230
How can I trust you

41:20.230 --> 41:22.315
when I know where you've been?

41:22.440 --> 41:23.983
My time in Arkham
gives you pause.

41:28.446 --> 41:29.948
I appreciate that.

41:31.574 --> 41:33.493
But I'm not the only one
with a past.

41:34.911 --> 41:37.122
I've done some digging
on you, Mr. Zhao.

41:38.081 --> 41:40.709
Before your father was driven
out of Taiwan by the CCP,

41:40.709 --> 41:42.502
he was a psychologist.
Isn't that right?

41:42.961 --> 41:44.629
- It is.
- Then you would agree

41:44.754 --> 41:47.507
that most drug use is rooted
in psychological need?

41:47.507 --> 41:50.301
I would agree that
everything humans do

41:50.427 --> 41:52.137
is rooted in psychological need.

41:53.263 --> 41:56.224
Then I would ask you to examine
this opportunity more closely.

42:01.021 --> 42:02.313
Look at them.

42:03.982 --> 42:06.484
Their city has been decimated.

42:07.819 --> 42:09.654
Our former mayor
was assassinated.

42:11.197 --> 42:13.199
A madman flooded our streets.

42:13.199 --> 42:14.576
[people laughing]

42:14.576 --> 42:16.202
[Sofia] People lost their homes.

42:16.202 --> 42:17.454
[phone buzzing]

42:17.454 --> 42:18.580
[Sofia] Their families.

42:19.497 --> 42:23.501
The world as they knew it
is gone.

42:24.294 --> 42:26.171
[Roxy] Hey! Bagman!

42:27.339 --> 42:28.340
[laughing]

42:30.508 --> 42:31.926
Come on, let's dance!

42:35.180 --> 42:36.890
[Victor] I have to get back
to work.

42:37.640 --> 42:38.683
Take a break.

42:44.147 --> 42:46.524
- [people cheering]
- [Victor] Roxy, really.

42:47.525 --> 42:48.860
[loud booming]

42:48.985 --> 42:50.153
[Graciela] The show's starting!

42:50.153 --> 42:51.696
[loud cheering]

42:51.821 --> 42:53.823
[intense dance music playing]

42:55.533 --> 42:56.993
[loud booming]

42:56.993 --> 42:58.870
[explosion echoing]

43:03.041 --> 43:05.502
- [explosions booming]
- [emotional music playing]

43:05.502 --> 43:07.295
- [rumbling]
- [shockwave whooshing]

43:07.295 --> 43:09.047
- [Victor grunts]
- [vials clinking]

43:13.176 --> 43:15.053
[loud booming]

43:22.352 --> 43:24.312
[high-pitched vibrations
sounding]

43:24.896 --> 43:27.899
[exhales, breathes rapidly]

43:30.360 --> 43:33.071
- [explosions continue]
- [people screaming]

43:36.533 --> 43:37.951
[water rushing]

43:38.076 --> 43:39.369
[sobbing]

43:39.369 --> 43:40.787
[soundscape distorting]

43:40.912 --> 43:43.289
[Victor continues sobbing]

43:46.084 --> 43:47.419
[Graciela] Victor...

43:47.544 --> 43:49.754
[intense dance music resumes]

43:50.547 --> 43:51.923
Victor!

43:53.133 --> 43:54.634
Honey, what is wrong with you?

43:54.759 --> 43:56.219
Shit's everywhere.

43:56.219 --> 43:58.972
- Keep it together. Alright?
- Yeah.

43:59.097 --> 44:00.140
Uh-huh.

44:01.224 --> 44:02.851
[vials clinking]

44:02.851 --> 44:04.853
[Sofia] These people need
to escape.

44:05.812 --> 44:08.732
And nothing delivers
a better escape than Bliss.

44:08.732 --> 44:09.941
[music quiets]

44:11.276 --> 44:12.944
That's why they
gave it to us in Arkham.

44:17.949 --> 44:21.453
It made us content, submissive.

44:23.079 --> 44:25.165
Any pain that we had
just floated away,

44:26.291 --> 44:28.626
allowing us to forget
where we were.

44:32.630 --> 44:34.466
It's a very powerful drug,

44:35.967 --> 44:38.845
and whoever controls it
will control

44:38.970 --> 44:42.307
the future of the drug trade
in Gotham.

44:50.023 --> 44:51.649
But if you are not interested...

44:53.026 --> 44:54.069
it's fine.

44:55.278 --> 44:57.530
I can go to the Neon Dragons
or the Odessa Mob.

44:57.530 --> 45:01.701
I, uh... I don't much care
who our sales reps are.

45:04.996 --> 45:06.998
[Oz scoffs] What the fuck
are you doin'?

45:07.540 --> 45:08.792
He's seen what we have.

45:09.668 --> 45:11.753
Make the deal or don't.
I'll be downstairs.

45:15.382 --> 45:17.717
- [water splashes]
- [breathing rapidly]

45:19.469 --> 45:21.471
[softly] Come on. Come on.

45:21.471 --> 45:23.765
[exhales, panting] Calm down.

45:24.391 --> 45:26.685
Calm down. Calm down.

45:26.810 --> 45:28.728
[dance music continues
in background]

45:28.853 --> 45:29.854
Okay.

45:30.522 --> 45:31.564
[phone buzzing]

45:39.322 --> 45:40.198
[door opens]

45:41.199 --> 45:43.201
[Oz] There he is.
Been lookin' for ya.

45:43.702 --> 45:45.495
The deal is done.
The Triads are in.

45:45.495 --> 45:47.372
Goddamn, it was sweet!

45:47.997 --> 45:49.791
We're so close
to the finish line, Vic,

45:49.791 --> 45:50.834
but we gotta play it safe.

45:50.834 --> 45:52.711
I still got the Maronis
on my ass.

45:53.336 --> 45:54.337
But you.

45:54.337 --> 45:55.380
You're the bagman.

45:55.880 --> 45:57.632
You held your own tonight.

45:57.632 --> 45:59.718
I'm proud of you, Vic.
Proud of you.

46:00.510 --> 46:02.512
Come on. I told Roxy
to order some bottles.

46:02.512 --> 46:04.848
- The good stuff.
- [phone buzzes]

46:05.515 --> 46:06.558
[Vic clears his throat]

46:08.727 --> 46:10.061
- Give it to me.
- Oz--

46:10.186 --> 46:11.479
Now, goddammit!

46:17.444 --> 46:18.820
You goin' somewhere?

46:20.363 --> 46:22.115
- With my fuckin' money?
- With the money?

46:22.240 --> 46:23.408
Whoa, no, I wouldn't--

46:23.533 --> 46:25.243
We're this fuckin' close!

46:25.368 --> 46:27.037
And you wanna bail?
For what? A piece of ass?

46:27.037 --> 46:29.039
- Oz, it's not her.
- [phone clatters]

46:29.039 --> 46:30.498
All right? It's not her. It's...

46:31.583 --> 46:32.834
It's the f--

46:32.834 --> 46:35.462
- It's the f-f...
- Jesus, kid!

46:35.462 --> 46:37.380
It's everything, alright?
It's everything.

46:37.380 --> 46:39.591
I do everything
that you ask me to do.

46:39.716 --> 46:41.259
Alright? I do it all. I try...

46:41.926 --> 46:43.803
I try to, at least.

46:43.803 --> 46:44.846
It's just...

46:48.475 --> 46:50.935
I-I don't know if I should.

46:51.061 --> 46:53.271
What?
You too good for this life?

46:53.396 --> 46:54.689
Huh? That it?

46:55.774 --> 46:56.941
That's funny, comin' from you.

46:58.568 --> 47:00.779
You wanna go,
what are ya waiting for?

47:00.904 --> 47:01.780
Fuckin' go.

47:03.406 --> 47:05.367
I c-- I can't leave.

47:06.951 --> 47:09.662
The fuck? You think I'm holdin'
you hostage or somethin'?

47:11.790 --> 47:13.291
That what?
You're my fuckin' prisoner?

47:14.584 --> 47:15.460
That it?

47:17.462 --> 47:19.506
- Hey, hey, hey.
- This what it feels like?

47:19.631 --> 47:20.799
- No.
- Being with me?

47:21.591 --> 47:23.468
- What did you have?
- Oz...

47:23.593 --> 47:25.095
Before I found you, huh, kid?

47:25.095 --> 47:26.888
[Victor] Hey, hey... Please...

47:26.888 --> 47:29.182
Fuckin' nothin', that's what.

47:29.307 --> 47:30.266
A loser.

47:30.266 --> 47:31.810
- I don't--
- A goddamn nobody.

47:31.935 --> 47:34.145
I gave you clothes, money,
a place to crash.

47:34.270 --> 47:37.232
You got all the opportunity
in the world right fuckin' here,

47:37.232 --> 47:38.483
for Christ's sake.

47:39.150 --> 47:40.235
But this.

47:43.196 --> 47:44.572
This is all you feel?

47:46.324 --> 47:48.159
You coulda left
whenever you wanted.

47:49.119 --> 47:50.537
But you chose to stay.

47:51.204 --> 47:53.665
- How 'bout you ask yourself why.
- [grunts]

47:54.290 --> 47:55.875
- Oz, I don't--
- Nah, let me help.

47:56.001 --> 47:57.043
You stayed

47:57.836 --> 47:59.504
'cause you want
somethin' better.

48:01.172 --> 48:02.966
You want more
than your father ever had.

48:02.966 --> 48:05.343
No. [sobbing]

48:05.468 --> 48:07.345
My dad would be ashamed of me.

48:07.470 --> 48:09.180
You wanna know
what's shameful, Vic?

48:10.515 --> 48:12.183
Workin' your whole goddamn life,

48:12.726 --> 48:14.519
having nothin' to show for it.

48:16.021 --> 48:17.689
You still think
there's good and bad?

48:18.398 --> 48:19.691
Right and wrong?

48:19.816 --> 48:20.734
There ain't.

48:20.859 --> 48:22.027
There's just this.

48:22.819 --> 48:24.195
Survival.

48:24.320 --> 48:25.864
Security. Pleasure.

48:27.907 --> 48:30.201
They don't give out awards
for dying in the projects.

48:30.869 --> 48:31.661
Fuck you.

48:31.661 --> 48:32.746
Fuck me?!

48:33.204 --> 48:34.998
Fuck the goddamn world!

48:34.998 --> 48:36.583
They don't give a shit about you

48:36.708 --> 48:38.043
or your family.

48:39.836 --> 48:41.880
You think you're nothin',
you are nothin'.

48:42.005 --> 48:44.299
Till the day you die.
I thought you were smart.

48:44.299 --> 48:46.051
But that's the life you want,
guess what, Vic?

48:46.176 --> 48:47.969
Good news. You already got it.

48:47.969 --> 48:50.055
[somber music playing]

48:51.765 --> 48:53.391
So go, get the fuck outta here.

48:54.100 --> 48:55.310
You don't deserve this.

49:07.364 --> 49:09.324
["Broken Belief" by Bob Moses
playing]

49:09.324 --> 49:11.534
[sirens wailing]

49:11.534 --> 49:13.745
[car engine sputtering]

49:24.130 --> 49:25.423
[car lock clicks]

49:29.260 --> 49:31.638
[engine starts, revs]

49:31.763 --> 49:33.098
[tires squeal]

49:34.557 --> 49:35.975
[ice rattling]

49:45.068 --> 49:47.612
♪ We live in the era
of purpose ♪

49:47.737 --> 49:49.989
♪ We live in the era of youth ♪

49:50.490 --> 49:52.909
♪ When the wise man's
warning is worthless ♪

49:52.909 --> 49:55.203
♪ I'm just a poor boy
begging for truth ♪

49:55.745 --> 49:58.289
♪ We live in the era
of purpose ♪

49:58.415 --> 50:00.917
♪ We live in the era of youth ♪

50:00.917 --> 50:03.461
♪ When the wise man's
warning is worthless ♪

50:03.461 --> 50:06.631
♪ I'm just a poor boy
begging for truth ♪

50:07.173 --> 50:10.760
♪ So, baby, you say
that we're free ♪

50:10.760 --> 50:12.470
♪ Oh, come on ♪

50:12.595 --> 50:16.099
♪ You've taken what
you wanted from me ♪

50:16.099 --> 50:17.642
♪ Ahh ♪

50:17.642 --> 50:19.644
♪ You've kept me ♪

50:19.769 --> 50:22.981
♪ Down on my knees
for so long ♪

50:23.106 --> 50:26.651
♪ A victim
of your broken belief ♪

50:26.776 --> 50:27.736
♪ Ahh ♪

50:38.246 --> 50:40.248
♪ Now there's a crack
in the surface ♪

50:40.248 --> 50:42.584
♪ Something dark
is seeping through ♪

50:43.168 --> 50:45.795
♪ We live in the land
of the many ♪

50:45.795 --> 50:48.048
♪ We live in the grip
of the few ♪

50:48.548 --> 50:51.009
♪ There's a poor girl
crying for justice ♪

50:51.134 --> 50:53.136
♪ There's a rich man
playing the fool ♪

50:53.762 --> 50:56.348
♪ All the wise men
longing for purpose ♪

50:56.473 --> 50:58.683
♪ And they're all just
looking to you ♪

50:59.893 --> 51:03.521
♪ So, baby, you say
that we're free ♪

51:03.521 --> 51:05.273
♪ Oh, come on... ♪

51:06.191 --> 51:08.068
[music continues inside club]

51:17.077 --> 51:17.952
Is it done?

51:18.536 --> 51:19.788
The Triads are in.

51:20.372 --> 51:21.247
[sniffs]

51:22.082 --> 51:23.375
You don't seem too excited.

51:25.251 --> 51:26.461
Trauma sells.

51:27.379 --> 51:29.047
Come on. We fuckin' did it.

51:29.506 --> 51:30.840
We should celebrate.

51:30.840 --> 51:33.426
I'm sure that you'll manage
just fine without me.

51:41.518 --> 51:42.852
Jesus Christ. Fine.

51:42.852 --> 51:44.062
I fucked you over.

51:45.271 --> 51:46.606
That what you wanna hear?

51:48.775 --> 51:50.985
Tell me that's not
your attempt at an apology.

51:52.195 --> 51:53.655
I didn't know
what Carmine would do.

51:54.364 --> 51:55.740
I knew somethin', but...

51:57.409 --> 51:58.451
fuckin' Arkham?

52:00.078 --> 52:01.413
His own flesh and blood?

52:04.916 --> 52:06.501
I swear, I thought
I was lookin' out for you.

52:06.501 --> 52:07.460
Bullshit.

52:08.128 --> 52:09.796
- You ratted me out.
- I ain't no rat!

52:09.921 --> 52:11.256
And I'm not the Hangman.

52:12.215 --> 52:14.759
You see the way people
look at me. Right?

52:16.302 --> 52:17.303
I know you do.

52:18.430 --> 52:20.098
And what was it all for? Hmm?

52:21.141 --> 52:22.684
For what? So you could what?

52:24.060 --> 52:25.270
Become a capo?

52:28.273 --> 52:29.941
You're not even a made man.

52:31.901 --> 52:33.278
Yeah, you're right.

52:34.070 --> 52:34.946
I ain't.

52:37.574 --> 52:39.284
I still made out
like a goddamn bandit.

52:39.409 --> 52:40.452
And you know what?

52:42.412 --> 52:43.663
It was worth it.

52:46.124 --> 52:47.042
You asked.

52:47.042 --> 52:48.460
That's my fuckin' answer.

52:48.585 --> 52:50.587
I got the club,
a Drops operation to run,

52:50.587 --> 52:51.963
my own thing.

52:55.008 --> 52:55.967
A guy like me?

52:56.593 --> 52:57.552
Gettin' all that?

52:58.511 --> 53:01.014
That don't mean nothin' to you,
but it does to me.

53:02.599 --> 53:04.309
Meant I could have
a better life.

53:07.771 --> 53:09.230
So yeah. Yeah.

53:11.691 --> 53:12.984
I don't regret what I got.

53:18.782 --> 53:20.325
[laughs softly]

53:22.535 --> 53:23.745
Wow.

53:24.329 --> 53:25.872
You know, but I am sorry.

53:28.667 --> 53:31.670
I'm fuckin' sorry for everything
that's happened to you.

53:33.380 --> 53:34.255
Jesus.

53:35.006 --> 53:36.299
You meant something to me.

53:36.299 --> 53:37.425
Still do.

53:39.552 --> 53:40.679
And I fucked it up.

53:41.471 --> 53:42.347
[sniffles]

53:44.849 --> 53:46.851
And that I ain't never
gonna live down.

53:55.360 --> 53:56.403
[sniffles]

54:17.257 --> 54:19.300
I don't know
where to go from here.

54:24.222 --> 54:25.849
I don't know how to trust you.

54:36.735 --> 54:38.194
How 'bout
I keep showin' you how.

54:38.194 --> 54:40.030
[vehicle approaching]

54:40.030 --> 54:42.741
[tires screeching]

54:45.035 --> 54:46.578
[man] Don't move.
Don't fucking move.

54:47.746 --> 54:49.622
[tense music playing]

54:51.416 --> 54:54.336
Oz, you think you can play us?

54:54.919 --> 54:58.340
We've been watching you, motherfucker.

55:00.216 --> 55:02.093
[percussive beat layers over
tense music]

55:09.851 --> 55:11.853
[emotional music playing]

55:27.952 --> 55:29.954
[emotional music swells]

55:35.919 --> 55:37.003
[gear shift clunks]

55:42.133 --> 55:43.468
Holy shit.

55:48.848 --> 55:50.684
- [tires squealing]
- [engine revs]

55:55.105 --> 55:56.272
[man groans]

55:56.272 --> 55:58.775
[car alarm wailing]

55:58.775 --> 55:59.693
[horn blaring]

55:59.818 --> 56:01.736
[groaning]

56:01.736 --> 56:04.322
[rapid percussive beat resumes]

56:11.454 --> 56:12.831
[gunshots]

56:13.873 --> 56:16.001
Kid, go!
We gotta fucking go! Now!

56:16.126 --> 56:17.419
W-What about Sofia?

56:17.419 --> 56:19.045
Fuck! Leave her.

56:19.170 --> 56:21.047
- [dramatic music playing]
- [engine revving]

56:22.882 --> 56:24.426
[tires screeching]

56:25.802 --> 56:27.554
[scattered gunfire]

56:27.554 --> 56:29.347
Goddammit, Vic!
I knew you'd come back!

56:29.472 --> 56:30.473
I fucking knew it!

56:30.473 --> 56:32.684
This is some fuckin' balls!

56:32.809 --> 56:34.436
That was incredible, kid.

56:34.436 --> 56:36.938
Jesus! We're in it now, Vic.
We're in it now.

56:36.938 --> 56:38.231
[music halts]

56:39.065 --> 56:41.860
["Me and the Devil"
by Gil Scott-Heron plays]

56:42.694 --> 56:44.487
♪ Me and the devil ♪

56:47.365 --> 56:50.035
♪ Walkin' side by side ♪

56:54.122 --> 56:55.790
♪ Me and the devil ♪

56:58.710 --> 57:01.254
♪ Walkin' side by side ♪

57:05.467 --> 57:08.553
♪ And I'm gonna see my woman ♪

57:09.763 --> 57:12.557
♪ Until I get satisfied ♪

57:16.936 --> 57:19.064
♪ See, see, you don't see why ♪

57:21.691 --> 57:24.235
♪ Like you'a dog me 'round ♪

57:28.948 --> 57:31.910
♪ You may bury my body ♪

57:33.495 --> 57:35.955
♪ Down by the highway side ♪

57:40.085 --> 57:43.254
♪ You may bury my body ♪

57:45.006 --> 57:47.759
♪ Down by the highway side ♪

57:51.596 --> 57:55.141
♪ So my old evil spirit can ♪

57:55.725 --> 57:58.645
♪ Catch a Greyhound bus
and ride ♪

58:06.152 --> 58:07.612
[music fades]

58:08.238 --> 58:11.032
[tense, dramatic music playing]

59:01.041 --> 59:03.001
[music fades]
